name w3-08-mig-alone-1
timeout 520
time 1991-01-19T00:00:00Z

# CAMPAIGN W3, SORTIE 8 OF 10 - THE SAME FIGHT WITH THE GROUND CONTROL DELETED.
# Spec, anchor and sources: doc/campaigns/w3-desert-storm.md. Format: doc/missions/campaign.md.
# CONTROL: w3-07-mig-cap.fbm. THE ONE THING THAT DIFFERS: the three `set brief_gci` lines are gone from
# all four MiG-29. Everything else - both packages, the load-outs, the ground set, the clock, the
# weather - is the control's, line for line. The cast is pairwise disjoint from the control's in every
# unit it can lose (`q8*` against `q7*`), which is rule 1 and not decoration: the campaign carry is keyed
# by callsign.
#
# THE ANCHOR'S OWN EXPLANATION OF A 6-FOR-0 RESULT, ISOLATED. Soviet doctrine assumed tight ground
# control, and the Iraqis flew "essentially alone, without the tactical architecture the design assumed"
# [T4]. In FlightBox that dependency is not a modifier but a TYPED, LATENCY-CHARGED COMMAND CHAIN: three
# entries over the MiG's own command bus, 8.0 s from the call to a radiating radar
# (doc/modules/mig29/datalink-gci.md, measured). Delete them and the N019 never receives its scan
# elevation, its range scale or its ZONE.
#
# THE POLICY THIS PAIR IS MEASURED UNDER IS DECLARED IN THE CONTROL'S HEADER AND REPEATED HERE, because
# four earlier campaigns ran this same deleted line and disagreed: `set n019_emission off`, the
# documented power-up state, which is O2's policy and not O1's or O5's. Under `off` the brief's third
# entry is the only thing in the tree that ever turns the radar on, so this file is not a badly aimed
# radar - it is a radar that never radiates. ATTRIBUTION RUN A3 is this file with that one token changed
# to `illum`, and it is what makes the claim a measurement instead of an inheritance.
#
# THE ARENA, the substitution and its direction, the layer this file measures, the night's cost and the
# time separation of the two engagements are stated in w3-07-mig-cap.fbm and hold unchanged.
#
# THE ONE TACTICAL QUESTION: HOW MUCH OF THE HISTORICAL 6-FOR-0 IS THE ARCHITECTURE AND HOW MUCH IS THE
# AIRCRAFT? One deleted line is the whole experiment, and the answer is a detection time.
#
# MEASURED (fingerprint 8cfb0b73f1ecdcbf), AND IT IS THE CONTROL'S EXACT MIRROR:
#   Red's first look   NEVER. ZERO `radar RADAR_CONTACT unit=q8mig*` lines in the whole run, against
#                      the control's 50
#   Red's shots        ZERO launch solutions, against the control's five. Every R-27R and R-73 lands
#                      back at base on the rail
#   Blue               unchanged to a tenth of a second: first solution t = 196.3 against 196.5. The
#                      controller does not move Blue's timeline at all; it decides whether Red is in the
#                      fight
#   the kill           `q8esca_aim120_6` on `q8mig1` at 8.94 m at t = 315.3 - 104.0 s LATER than the
#                      control's, because Blue had to run its target down instead of meeting it
#   the strike         2 of 2 released at t = 174.6 / 190.0, byte-identical ticks to the control's
#   the run            ends t = 370.4, 97.6 s longer than the control's
# THE CONTROLLER IS WORTH THE ENTIRE ENGAGEMENT ON AN AIRCRAFT THAT STARTS SILENT - which is O2's
# result and NOT O1's or O5's, and W3 is the first campaign to measure BOTH POLICIES IN ONE ROUND.
# ATTRIBUTION RUN A3 is this file with `set n019_emission illum`: 50 Red contacts, 7 launch solutions,
# `q8mig1` killed at the SAME t = 272.8 run end as the control - i.e. under `illum` the deleted brief
# costs NOTHING measurable, and under `off` it costs everything. The lever is the emission policy, and
# the four earlier campaigns that disagreed were each right about their own file.
#
# WHAT TO READ:
#   events.log      the count of `radar RADAR_CONTACT unit=q8mig*` lines - in the control it is 20, and
#                   what it is here is the answer; then `sms LAUNCH_SOLUTION` per side
#   telemetry_q8mig1.csv  the antenna and emission columns: a radar that was never switched on
#
# READING RULE: exit 3 = TIMEOUT is expected; this file is a measuring rig. THE MEASUREMENT IS THE
# TRIPLE (first Red radar contact, Red shots, Red arrivals) read beside w3-07-mig-cap.fbm. A run in
# which Red still shoots would falsify the campaign's prediction and would be the more interesting
# result; it is reported either way.

net kari8
  control q8nod
  link wire
  period 4.0
  hold 3
  wcs free
  member q8nod
  member q8flk autonomy hold

unit q8stra
  module f16
  team friendly
  flight st8 1
  spawn 33.20000 43.85000 5000 90.0 450
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 80
  set fcr_mode off
  set attack_mode ccrp
  set rwr on
  set datalink on
  set store 3 mk84
  set store 7 mk84
  set cmds_mode auto
  set cmds_program 1
  set cmds_chaff 60
  set cmds_flare 60
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task attack
  wp 33.20000 44.36000 5000 450
  wp 33.20000 43.90000 5000 450
  objective kill unit q8tgt
  objective survive

